WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:07.620
Djinns in love, excrement-soaked billionaires,&nbsp;
and a musical action epic that puts the MCU to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:14.280
shame. 2022's best films covered every genre and&nbsp;
proved that original stories are far from dead.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.740
Athena is a thriller, a family drama, and&nbsp;
a snapshot of contemporary tensions between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:24.120
citizens and institutions. It's all told from&nbsp;
the perspective of three grieving brothers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.920
trying to make sense of their fourth brother's&nbsp;
death. If the opening sequence doesn't grab you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.000
you may not have a pulse: In&nbsp;
a continuous 10 minute shot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.400
a press conference regarding the brother’s murder&nbsp;
by the police collapses into a frenetic raid of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.620
the station by well-organized protestors,&nbsp;
who proceed to fortify an apartment complex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.873
into a revolutionary stronghold. It&nbsp;
only gets more intense from there.

00:00:49.432 --> 00:00:51.360
Years after the release of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.820
acclaimed debut feature In Bruges, writer-director&nbsp;
Martin McDonagh reunites stars Colin Farrell and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:02.760
Brendan Gleeson for another bizarre and moody dark&nbsp;
comedy. Set on a fictional island off the coast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.460
of Ireland in the 1920s, where drinking, music,&nbsp;
and idle chat are the only available pastimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.560
The Banshees of Inisherin is the story of a messy&nbsp;
breakup between lifelong friends Colm and Pádraic.

00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:19.086
"Let's just call it quits."
"We won't call it quits. We'll call it the start."

00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:24.660
Witty, bleakly funny, and shot on the&nbsp;
picturesque Aran Islands, The Banshees of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:30.333
Inisherin is a shoe-in for Oscar nominations&nbsp;
for acting, writing, and costume design.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:31.020
Now and then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.360
a horror film comes along that has to be seen to&nbsp;
be believed. Barbarian is one such movie. A woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.860
arrives at the house she's renting for a short&nbsp;
period of time, only to discover someone's already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:46.200
home. Now, she must spend the night sharing the&nbsp;
home with this stranger. That's not all: The house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.500
itself seems to harbor its own strange secrets.&nbsp;
Equal parts shocking, revolting, and hilarious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.800
Barbarian is best enjoyed without spoilers and&nbsp;
a room full of likewise unsuspecting viewers.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.440
The streets of Gotham City have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.960
never been grittier than in The Batman, a new&nbsp;
interpretation of DC's most popular superhero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.360
Despite being yet another reboot that takes the&nbsp;
character "back to basics" as a lone crimefighter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.760
chasing gangsters and serial killers, The Batman&nbsp;
still feels distinct from both Christopher Nolan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.520
nuts-and-bolts realism and Tim Burton's dark&nbsp;
whimsy. More than any previous Batman film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:30.360
it's a detective story, closer to a 1970s neo-noir&nbsp;
than a modern action blockbuster. Within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:36.480
film's ambitious three-hour runtime you'll find&nbsp;
memorable performances, gorgeous photography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.628
and one of the most in-depth explorations of&nbsp;
the title character ever to hit the big screen.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.880
2018's Black Panther was a global sensation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:50.520
earning over $1 billion at the box office&nbsp;
and a slew of Academy Award nominations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.440
including Best Picture. As with any successful&nbsp;
chapter in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.200
it seemed obvious that Black Panther would expand&nbsp;
into a colossal franchise in its own right. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.580
sudden and tragic death of star Chadwick Boseman&nbsp;
threw the future of the series into question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.020
but director Ryan Coogler and his cast and&nbsp;
crew committed themselves to reworking the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.200
planned sequel into a heartfelt&nbsp;
tribute to their absent friend.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.600
On top of the familiar action, adventure, and&nbsp;
spectacle that Marvel fans have come to expect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:23.760
Black Panther: Wakanda Forever offers a&nbsp;
complex meditation on grief, following the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.980
lovable ensemble from the first film through the&nbsp;
process of moving on after a devastating loss.

00:03:29.406 --> 00:03:30.420
Belle follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:35.520
a talented teenage songwriter, Suzu, who's&nbsp;
been unable to raise her voice in song since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.420
the tragic death of her mother. But when&nbsp;
she logs into the futuristic social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:45.960
platform "U," Suzu transforms into "Belle," a&nbsp;
spellbinding songstress who becomes a global&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.340
sensation overnight. As Suzu attempts&nbsp;
to reconcile the two parts of herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:56.160
she becomes fascinated by an infamous online&nbsp;
prizefighter with a monstrous virtual avatar.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.440
Belle is nominally an adaptation of the classic&nbsp;
fairy tale Beauty and the Beast for the social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.900
media age, but the film brings far more to&nbsp;
the table than just the familiar beats of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:13.260
source material. Belle is part timeless and part&nbsp;
bleeding-edge contemporary, as exemplified by its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:19.800
two distinct but equally beautiful art styles —&nbsp;
painterly traditional animation to represent the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:26.152
real world and eye-popping cell-shaded CGI to&nbsp;
represent the virtual reality of the Internet.

00:04:26.152 --> 00:04:27.900
Cooper Raiff stars opposite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.820
Dakota Johnson in Cha Cha Real Smooth, a&nbsp;
sweet, witty indie comedy that took home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:38.040
the U.S. Dramatic Audience Award at 2022's&nbsp;
Sundance Film Festival. Raiff portrays Andrew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:42.720
a recent college graduate who's landed back at&nbsp;
his mom and stepdad's house while he figures out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:47.280
the next phase of his life. Though built around&nbsp;
the sizzling chemistry between Andrew and Dakota&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.500
Johnson's 30-something character Domino, Cha&nbsp;
Cha Real Smooth is really a quirky and heartfelt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:58.693
coming-of-age story about a college-educated young&nbsp;
adult who has to get a job at the mall food court.

00:04:58.693 --> 00:05:00.240
South Korean director Park&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.700
Chan-wook of Oldboy and The Handmaiden fame&nbsp;
presents a seductive thriller that expertly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:11.220
balances suspense, romance, and comedy in&nbsp;
Decision to Leave. When an ace detective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.900
is assigned to investigate a mysterious&nbsp;
death, he becomes bizarrely obsessed with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:20.940
the victim's widow. The feeling seems to&nbsp;
be mutual, but is the widow simply toying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:26.100
with him to cover up a murder? Gorgeously shot&nbsp;
and simmering with tension that's occasionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.428
broken by a pitch-perfect gag, Decision&nbsp;
to Leave is a masterfully crafted mystery.

00:05:31.428 --> 00:05:32.580
Around the turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.180
of the millennium, a string of teen&nbsp;
flicks adapting the plays of William&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.300
Shakespeare to a contemporary&nbsp;
high school setting debuted.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.160
"Sweet love, renew thy force."

00:05:43.931 --> 00:05:46.080
"Hey! Don't say s— like that&nbsp;
to me. People can hear you."

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:51.240
With Do Revenge, director Jennifer Kaytin&nbsp;
Robinson makes a killer case for giving the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:57.060
same treatment to the films of Alfred Hitchcock.&nbsp;
In this comedy-thriller loosely based on Strangers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:01.860
on a Train, a new kid at an affluent prep&nbsp;
school and its disgraced queen bee team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:06.540
up to exact some cruel and imaginative&nbsp;
vengeance upon each others' enemies.

00:06:07.819 --> 00:06:09.600
"I want to burn her to the ground."

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:15.120
"Woah. You're giving off some serious Glenn&nbsp;
Close and 'Fatal Attraction' energy.'"

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:21.300
Lively, funny, and sporting a tremendous&nbsp;
performance from Maya Hawke, if Do Revenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:25.480
doesn't spark a new trend in high school&nbsp;
thrillers, someone is going to pay.

00:06:25.853 --> 00:06:27.480
Emily the Criminal is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:32.700
crime thriller born of the present moment, as&nbsp;
a generation weighed down by debt and denied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:39.120
full-time employment struggles to make ends meet&nbsp;
in the "gig economy." Aubrey Plaza stars as Emily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:44.220
who juggles various menial jobs with combined&nbsp;
wages that can't make a dent in her student&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:49.140
loans. When presented with the opportunity&nbsp;
to make a lot of money fast, Emily becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:54.540
a "dummy shopper," maxing out cloned credit cards&nbsp;
and reselling the purchases on the black market.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:57.240
"You know what my mistake really&nbsp;
was? I didn't go far enough."

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:01.080
The story of a hard-luck outlaw&nbsp;
getting in too deep is nothing new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.425
but Emily the Criminal has such a&nbsp;
modern edge that it can't be denied.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:08.760
Evelyn Wang is an exhausted and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.540
unfulfilled laundromat owner who's&nbsp;
just trying to get her taxes done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:17.820
when she's suddenly recruited to fight in an&nbsp;
inter-dimensional war. To save the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:22.260
Evelyn will have to learn how to "verse-jump,"&nbsp;
tapping into the feelings, memories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:27.540
and skills of her alternate selves, all of whom&nbsp;
have done more with their lives than she has.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:35.340
Everything Everywhere All at Once is uproariously&nbsp;
funny, visually dazzling, and deeply moving.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.600
Director Steven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:41.880
Spielberg has shaped the past 50 years of&nbsp;
cinema more than any other filmmaker. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:47.100
he's finally ready to tell the story of the&nbsp;
events that shaped Steven Spielberg. Though his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:52.320
films are generally known for their sincerity, The&nbsp;
Fabelmans is Spielberg's most personal work yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:56.160
as a semi-autobiographical story&nbsp;
based on his own adolescence.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.953
"You do what your heart says you have to."

00:07:58.953 --> 00:08:03.960
Sammy Fabelman is a young Jewish kid with&nbsp;
a love of filmmaking who must navigate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:09.180
collapse of his parents' marriage. His is a sweet&nbsp;
coming-of-age story that's also a thoughtful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:14.400
and sympathetic examination of a loving couple&nbsp;
who've drawn apart from each other. Beyond this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:19.800
The Fabelmans is a charming love letter to&nbsp;
cinema, following its protagonist as he embarks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.707
on ever more complicated home movie projects&nbsp;
that are a delight to see on the big screen.

00:08:25.426 --> 00:08:26.760
The latest in a proud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:32.880
tradition of modernized Jane Austen adaptations,&nbsp;
Fire Island sets Pride and Prejudice during a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.080
tight-knit, queer chosen family's annual&nbsp;
reunion at the titular New York vacation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:42.060
spot. Austen's novel of manners translates&nbsp;
beautifully into this contemporary setting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:48.120
trading prim propriety for raunchy comedy, while&nbsp;
also poking fun at the roles of race, class, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:55.140
narrow beauty standards in a closed but thriving&nbsp;
sexual economy. Conrad Ricamora is a standout as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.140 --> 00:09:01.080
Will, Fire Island's version of the steamy and&nbsp;
stoic Mr. Darcy, but the heart of the film is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:06.120
the friendship between the lead characters,&nbsp;
portrayed by Joel Kim Booster and Bowen Yang.

00:09:06.573 --> 00:09:08.940
Fire of Love tells the true story of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:14.820
Katia and Maurice Krafft, fearless volcanologists&nbsp;
who visited multiple erupting volcanoes during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:20.040
the latter half of the 20th century. To finance&nbsp;
their studies, the couple filmed and photographed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:25.380
their adventures, turning them into books and&nbsp;
movies that captivated audiences across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:30.780
world. This documentary is the distillation of&nbsp;
hundreds of hours of footage of their strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:36.900
journey into one, stunning narrative. Fire of&nbsp;
Love is part nature documentary, part romance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.400
and part tragedy, best seen with the&nbsp;
person next to you clutching your hand.

00:09:41.853 --> 00:09:44.580
Set in Mussolini's fascist Italy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:50.700
Guillermo del Toro's Pinocchio is a dark fairy&nbsp;
tale about childhood, parenthood, and mortality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:55.740
brought to life via stunning stop-motion&nbsp;
animation. What's most remarkable about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.900
film is that it's family entertainment that never&nbsp;
panders too hard to either adults or children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:06.960
There are heavy themes and silly slapstick, but&nbsp;
neither feels like a correction for the other. Del&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:12.600
Toro is a grown-up with a kid's imagination,&nbsp;
equally capable of simplifying complex ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:18.240
and extracting the maximum substance from&nbsp;
storybook concepts. The result is one the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:24.360
year's best animated features, and a worthy entry&nbsp;
in the filmography of the Oscar-winning director.

00:10:24.786 --> 00:10:25.440
In between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:28.980
bringing his friends on vacations&nbsp;
to sunny locales around the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:33.660
Adam Sandler maintains a successful&nbsp;
career as a dramatic actor. In Hustle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:39.180
Sandler plays a desperate basketball scout who&nbsp;
discovers a world-class talent in a poor single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:44.760
dad from Spain. The film doesn't exactly break&nbsp;
the sports drama mold, but Sandler and co-star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:51.180
Juancho Hernangómez share a lovely chemistry that&nbsp;
reminds you how uplifting this dying genre can be.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.220
"This is all for you, pal."

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.300
"It's for us."

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.440
"Okay, it's for us."

00:10:55.706 --> 00:10:56.940
The Menu is a satirical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:01.860
thriller in which a dozen discerning diners&nbsp;
catch a ferry ride to an exclusive culinary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:07.800
experience that just might be their last. The&nbsp;
film has a bit of a Twilight Zone edge to it:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:14.100
Its ironic twists are somewhat predictable,&nbsp;
but also hugely satisfying. Like a great meal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:19.560
it's almost exactly what you ordered, but with&nbsp;
a few surprising accents and secret ingredients&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:25.666
to make what could have been simple sustenance&nbsp;
into an experience worth playing top dollar for.

00:11:25.666 --> 00:11:31.200
Horror&nbsp;&nbsp; auteur Jordan Peele returns with his&nbsp;
biggest and most ambitious film yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:37.500
a sci-fi-horror-comedy-Western that deconstructs&nbsp;
the very concept of filmed entertainment. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.940
a brother-sister pair of down-on-their-luck&nbsp;
horse trainers spies a UFO above their ranch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:46.980
they hope to secure their legacy by capturing the&nbsp;
first incontrovertible proof of extraterrestrial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:52.440
life. But at what cost are they willing to attain&nbsp;
the impossible shot? And what drives people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:58.020
seek out bizarre spectacle in the first place?&nbsp;
Peele doesn't answer every question he poses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:06.000
to tremendous effect. Expect the wheels in your&nbsp;
head to keep turning for days after you see Nope.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.560
From celebrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:13.980
director Robert Eggers comes this unflinchingly&nbsp;
brutal historical fantasy, based on the ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:19.740
Viking epic that inspired Shakespeare's Hamlet.&nbsp;
The dethroned Prince Amleth will stop at nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:25.620
to exact vengeance against the uncle who slew&nbsp;
his father and kidnapped his mother — but will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:31.500
his quest leave him more beast than man? The&nbsp;
Northman is as visually stunning as it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:38.266
disturbing, a meticulous and unsanitized&nbsp;
portrait of the grim and miserable past.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.720
Prey, a prequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:43.440
to Predator set in the North American&nbsp;
Great Plains during the 18th century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:49.440
is by far the best installment in the&nbsp;
series since the original. It's a lean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:56.100
character-driven horror-thriller with some gnarly,&nbsp;
cleverly staged violence. Amber Midthunder makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:01.260
her mark on action cinema as Naru, a young&nbsp;
Comanche warrior looking to prove herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:06.960
by hunting a dangerous beast. Her prey turns&nbsp;
out to be a well-armed extraterrestrial who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:12.240
come to kill humans for sport, as well as a&nbsp;
portent of the colonizing threat that awaits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:16.620
her community. Like all Predator films,&nbsp;
Prey can be enjoyed entirely on its own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:21.660
but it also contains some cute Easter eggs for&nbsp;
longtime fans of the franchise's mythology.

00:13:22.219 --> 00:13:23.700
Resurrection is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:28.260
white-knuckle psychological horror film&nbsp;
in which star Rebecca Hall delivers one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:34.320
of 2022's best performances. Hall portrays&nbsp;
Margaret, a businesswoman and single parent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:40.560
who seems in total control of her life until a&nbsp;
mysterious man from her past resurfaces and sends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:46.980
her spiraling into an all-consuming panic.&nbsp;
What is it that makes his mere presence so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:52.686
terrifying? We are absolutely not telling&nbsp;
— you need to see this one for yourself.

00:13:52.686 --> 00:13:56.220
Essentially a superhero epic based on two real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.220 --> 00:14:02.880
Indian revolutionaries of the 1920s who likely&nbsp;
never actually met, RRR is a violent, thrilling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:09.180
heartfelt, and gleefully over-the-top Tollywood&nbsp;
action/musical blockbuster. Its song and dance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:15.960
number "Naatu Naatu" has gone mega-viral online,&nbsp;
and it teases only a small fraction the bombastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:22.260
excitement of its battle scenes. It's a three-hour&nbsp;
film that energizes rather than exhausts its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:26.460
audience. By the time the credits roll, you'll&nbsp;
feel like you could punch a hole through the moon.

00:14:27.073 --> 00:14:29.160
Just as each Scream sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:33.780
has commented on the nature of horror sequels&nbsp;
and the changing landscape of horror cinema,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:39.900
this fifth entry tackles the contemporary trend&nbsp;
of the "requel," in which "legacy characters"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:44.520
pass the torch to a new generation.&nbsp;
But, as always, Scream isn't just about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:49.620
dorky inside jokes for cinephiles, it's also a&nbsp;
thrilling horror "whodunnit" in its own right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:55.080
with scares and chuckles in equal measure.&nbsp;
Scream can be enjoyed as either a jumping-on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:00.480
point or a satisfying conclusion to one&nbsp;
of horror's most consistent franchises.

00:15:01.039 --> 00:15:02.400
Cate Blanchett delivers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:08.220
one of the most captivating performances of her&nbsp;
career as fictional composer-conductor Lydia Tár&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:14.220
in this gripping character study. Tár is a titan&nbsp;
in the world of classical music, with a colossal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:19.620
ego to match. But in the run-up to her latest&nbsp;
career milestone, whispers of her personal and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:24.900
professional misconduct crescendo into a deafening&nbsp;
roar that threatens to knock her off her podium.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:29.040
Blanchett endows Tár with&nbsp;
such charisma and menace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:35.100
one can immediately understand how awful&nbsp;
people manage to acquire so much power — or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:39.780
how power can make a person awful. There&nbsp;
are moments when you might find yourself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:46.107
sympathizing with this self-obsessed genius,&nbsp;
even as you eagerly anticipate her downfall.

00:15:46.107 --> 00:15:48.420
With Three Thousand Years of Longing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:54.300
director George Miller has delivered a haunting&nbsp;
adult fairy tale romance. Though unsurprisingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.300 --> 00:16:00.300
a box office bomb, this dark storybook tale of&nbsp;
a solitary academic who frees a lonely djinn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:04.860
from centuries of imprisonment is both&nbsp;
thought-provoking and heart-wrenching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:10.080
musing on the nature of love, the shape&nbsp;
of stories, and the death of myth in our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:14.820
modern world. It's not a "feel good"&nbsp;
movie, it's a "feel everything" movie.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.680
Till is based on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:21.600
true story of Mamie Till's fight for justice after&nbsp;
her son, Emmett, was brutally murdered by white&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:27.600
supremacists at the age of 14. Till introduces us&nbsp;
to a bright and charming young man in Emmett "Bo"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:33.900
Till, and forces us to reckon with his inhuman&nbsp;
death and the deep wounds it leaves behind — not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:39.780
only on those who love him, but on everyone the&nbsp;
lynching is meant to terrorize. An intimate and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:45.480
heartbreaking character study, it centers on&nbsp;
a woman whose unimaginable pain becomes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:52.080
center of a national news story and a movement for&nbsp;
civil rights. What results is a commanding entry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:57.240
to the Hollywood main stage for both director&nbsp;
Chinonye Chukwu and star Danielle Deadwyler.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.220
Top Gun: Maverick is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:05.880
a ridiculously fun cinematic novelty that will&nbsp;
thrill even the most cynical viewer. Eschewing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:11.700
CGI as much as possible, director Joseph&nbsp;
Kosinski puts the actors and cameras right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:18.540
into actual fighter jets and lets audiences marvel&nbsp;
at incredible real-life feats of aerial agility.

00:17:18.886 --> 00:17:20.746
"Just want to manage expectations."

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:26.820
The spectacle is bound together by irresistible&nbsp;
charisma machine Tom Cruise reprising the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:31.359
of Pete "Maverick" Mitchell, leading a new&nbsp;
generation of hot shots into the danger zone.

00:17:31.359 --> 00:17:34.020
Writer-director Ruben Östlund won his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:40.440
second Palme d'Or for Triangle of Sadness, a wacky&nbsp;
satire about class disparity and the apocalypse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:46.800
Though its first and third acts contain plenty&nbsp;
of laughs, its middle hour — set on a luxury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:52.440
yacht populated by sociopathic billionaires and an&nbsp;
exhausted staff — is worth the price of admission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:58.800
alone. Essentially a broad gross-out comedy for&nbsp;
arthouse audiences, Triangle of Sadness captures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:04.080
the lunacy of the mega-rich. It's not the most&nbsp;
subtle film of the year, but it is the only one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:09.900
that offers the thrill of watching the soulless&nbsp;
elite violently evacuate their digestive tracts.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.000
Overachieving eighth-grader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:16.980
Mei Lee awakens one morning to discover&nbsp;
she’s transformed into a giant red panda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:22.140
just as every woman in her family has&nbsp;
for generations. Mei's panda form emerges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:26.580
whenever she experiences strong emotions, and&nbsp;
her mother Ming expects her to rein it in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:32.340
like she did. But what if Mei likes being an&nbsp;
excitable furry monster? Turning Red is a joyful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:37.920
celebration of friendship, family, and how the&nbsp;
awkward process of growing up complicates both.

00:18:38.266 --> 00:18:40.020
The Woman King is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:45.000
a grand Hollywood war epic unlike any&nbsp;
other. Set in 19th century Dahomey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:50.914
it stars Viola Davis as General Nanisca, the&nbsp;
leader of an elite army of female soldiers.

00:18:50.914 --> 00:18:54.100
"Fight or we die."

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:59.160
Through the eyes of Nanisca&nbsp;
and teenage recruit Nawi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:03.840
The Woman King explores the lives of these&nbsp;
incredible warriors as their nation attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:08.280
to divest itself from the monstrosity of&nbsp;
the slave trade. Between its taut direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:15.060
gnarly action, and heartfelt performances, it's&nbsp;
a prestige blockbuster that kicks butt while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:19.380
celebrating a piece of history Hollywood&nbsp;
has traditionally failed to represent.

